 "assessment": {
  "name": "Agnew Relationship Measure – 5 (ARM-5)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Agnew Relationship Measure – 5 (ARM-5; Cahill et al., 2012) is a five-item, client-rated measure of the therapeutic alliance, developed as a short form of the 28-item ARM (Agnew-Davies et al., 1998). Completed in under a minute by clients aged 18 and over, it is designed for repeated use in Feedback Informed Treatment, where clinicians gather brief feedback on the working relationship and use it to adjust care while therapy is underway (Miller et al., 2016).",
